we recently got to preview team ninjas  neo2 and it's very much a continuation  of the methodical soul style samurai  combat from the original set several  decades before the first game you play  as a nameless samurai who defies death  by merging with a yokai spirit as a  being of both the human and demon worlds  your custom character is able to use  both conventional human weapons like  katanas Spears in the new transformer  will switch glaive along with a suite of  demonic attacks that channel the spirits  of slain yokai while neo2 sticks close  to the foundation set by its predecessor  a lot of attention has been given to  refining the core combat the online  co-op gameplay and how you develop and  evolve your character as they explore  Sengoku era Japan from our recent  hands-on gameplay where we explored a  castle overrun by demons and rogue ninja  it was clear that the high-stress  gameplay remains intact which included  all those pesky sudden deaths that are  entirely your fault because you weren't  paying attention to your surroundings  still I'd say that the section of neo to  be played is fair in how it throws  challenges your way due to the number of  tools and skills you've got at your  disposal continuing on from the original  games Diablo style RPG loot system and  character building set up the sequel  takes things further with an overhauled  skill and ability system that allows you  to develop your hero in ways that best  reflect your style want to stick with  your learnings of proper samurai  patience and resolve you can do that or  perhaps you want to lean more into the  teachings of the ninja and own mule  allowing you to buff your weapons with  elemental damage you can certainly  follow those paths as well but what  really makes neo to so different from  the original is the addition of yokai  powers after slaying powerful demons  throughout the world you'll be able to  claim their souls to elevate your  strength in battle there's something  especially satisfying about slaying a  powerful demon and then claiming their  soul for yourself by using these  abilities in combat you're able to  exploit and opponent's weakness opening  them up for several quick and powerful  strikes but when things get particularly  hairy you're also able to enter a full  on yokai state which significantly  amplifies your strength and agility one  demon form you take on for example who  wields a set of daggers grants you a  useful - move that can get you out of  trouble in a pinch following a round of  alpha and beta tests developer team  ninja has refined to the core gameplay  even more these changes include tweaking  boss attacks and amplifying the  effectiveness of weapons which will  hopefully make the final game a bit more  even while the difficulty has always  been a point of contention for soul  style games neo - doesn't totally send  you up the river without a paddle  there are far more options for you to  take advantage of here which helps  overcoming the many harrowing encounters  ultimately feel more satisfying than the  original set for release on march 13th  neo - sticks close to what made the  original game great while also fleshing  out its own identity there's so much  going on in neo - but well let this  gameplay speak for itself in the  following footage we show off more  exploration of the castle the various  combat skills your character has and  what sort of strange events you can find  when going on  the beaten path  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]
 

